--
N5008 [temp.deduct.type]/9, Example 4: S<int, const int &, const int &>
matches `S<T1, const Z &...>' with Z = {int, int}.  The front end selected
the primary template (bin53): disambiguate_template_classes bound a
trailing pack only when the pattern was a bare `Z...'.  A pattern is now
compared with each remaining argument, each comparison deducing the next
element (deduce_trailing_type_pack_pattern).  test_patterns.desc: `Z *...',
`L<Z>...', a pattern naming another parameter, and mismatches.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
